{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Thus, etc.</b> The reason for 'YHWH of Hosts' is on account of 'the steward,' who is appointed over the royal palace, as though he is the officer in charge of the treasury that is stored up:" "<b>Steward.</b> Like 'store-cities' (Exodus 1:11), like treasuries:" "The sense of <b>concerning</b> is that he should prophesy concerning him and say to him:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:40.786004417Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}